"><span class="enc-name">House of David</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">The House of David was the dynasty that, according to the Hebrew Bible, descended from King David and ruled the Kingdom of Judah from Jerusalem for about four…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/house-of-dreux"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/house-of-dreux.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">House of Dreux</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The House of Dreux was a cadet branch of the French royal Capetian dynasty, descended from Robert I, Count of Dreux, a son of Louis VI.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/house-of-eggenberg"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/house-of-eggenberg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">House of Eggenberg</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The House of Eggenberg was an Austrian noble family from Graz that rose to great wealth in Habsburg service.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/house-of-elders-somaliland"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/house-of-elders-somaliland.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">House of Elders (Somaliland)</span><span class="enc-type">Institution</span><span class="enc-snip">The Guurti, or House of Elders, is the upper chamber of the parliament of Somaliland, made up of clan elders and their representatives.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/house-of-eppenstein"><span class="enc-name">House of Eppenstein</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Eppensteiners were a noble family from Styria who held the Duchy of Carinthia, together with the March of Verona, for long periods between 1011 and 1122.</span></a