raine</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The House of Habsburg-Lorraine was the dynasty founded by the marriage in 1736 of Maria Theresa, heiress of the Habsburg lands, and Francis Stephen, duke of Lorraine…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/house-of-hanover"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/house-of-hanover.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">House of Hanover</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The House of Hanover was a German princely dynasty, electors and later kings of Hanover, that ruled Great Britain and Ireland from 1714 to 1901.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/house-of-haro"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/house-of-haro.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">House of Haro</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The House of Haro was a Castilian noble family that ruled the Lordship of Biscay from the 11th to the 14th century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/house-of-hasan-jalalyan"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/house-of-hasan-jalalyan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">House of Hasan-Jalalyan</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Hasan-Jalalyans were an Armenian princely family of Khachen in Artsakh, descended from Hasan-Jalal Dawla, who ruled in the 13th century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/house-of-hauteville"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/house-of-hauteville.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">House of Hauteville</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The House of Hauteville was a Norman family fro